# Local development. In production every one of these is a Workers SECRET
# (`wrangler secret put NAME`) — never a `var` in wrangler.jsonc, which is
# committed to a public repo.

# ---------- Required ----------
# Signs the session cookie. Any long random string; changing it logs everyone out.
AUTH_SECRET=any-long-random-string
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# There is no DATABASE_URL. State lives in Cloudflare D1, bound as `DB` in
# wrangler.jsonc, one JSON row per user. Locally, with no binding present,
# lib/db.ts falls back to an in-memory store that resets on restart.

# ---------- Accounts ----------
# Username/password, one env pair per account. A slot missing either half is
# skipped entirely and can never match, so unused slots need no value.
# Kid slots: KID, KID2, KID3, KID4, KID5 — adding an account is two secrets
# and a deploy, no code change.
KID_USERNAME=
KID_PASSWORD=
# KID2_USERNAME=
# KID2_PASSWORD=
PARENT_USERNAME=
PARENT_PASSWORD=

# Set to "google" to disable password login entirely. Anything else (or unset)
# leaves username/password enabled.
# AUTH_MODE=

# ---------- Google sign-in (optional) ----------
# Only needed with AUTH_MODE=google. The callback is derived from APP_ORIGIN.
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
# APP_ORIGIN=https://your-app.example.com

# ---------- AI provider ----------
# "openai" (default) or "gemini", via its OpenAI-compatible endpoint, so no
# other code changes. See docs/01-decisions.md D-011.
AI_PROVIDER=openai

# Per-provider defaults live in lib/openai.ts. Note that gpt-5.x rejects a
# custom `temperature` — lib/openai.ts strips it rather than sending one.
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.5
# OPENAI_MODEL_CHEAP=gpt-5-mini

# ---------- Content filter (spec 09) ----------
# Only needed with AI_PROVIDER=gemini — the Gemini compat layer has no
# /moderations route. On OpenAI this falls back to OPENAI_API_KEY.
# MODERATION_API_KEY=sk-...

# ---------- Alerts (spec 05, spec 09) ----------
# PARENT_EMAIL is a secret, not a var: it is a personal inbox. The sender
# address is the ALERT_FROM var in wrangler.jsonc, restricted by the
# send_email binding so a compromised Worker cannot spoof other addresses.
PARENT_EMAIL=
# KID_EMAIL=

# ---------- Dev only ----------
# Loads the invented fixture in lib/seed.ts so UI work skips discovery.
# Guarded by NODE_ENV, so a production build ignores it.
# SEED_DEMO=1

# Points the SDK at test/mock-openai.js.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3200
# PROBE_MODEL=gpt-5-mini
